{"id":"notre-dame-de-paris","name":"Notre-Dame de Paris","qid":"Q2981","country":"France","locality":"4th arrondissement of Paris, Quartier Notre-Dame","lat":"48.853","lon":"2.3498","built":"1163","year":1163,"year_text":"1163","century":"12th century","era":"Middle Ages","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"French Gothic architecture; Rayonnant; classic gothic; Early Gothic architecture","heritage":"classified historical monument","type":"minor basilica; Catholic cathedral","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notre-Dame_de_Paris","text":"Notre-Dame de Paris (French: Cathédrale Notre-Dame de Paris French: [nɔtʁ(ə) dam də paʁi]: \"Cathedral of Our Lady of Paris\"), often referred to simply as Notre-Dame, is a medieval Catholic cathedral and basilica on the Île de la Cité (an island in the River Seine), in the 4th arrondissement of Paris, France. It is the cathedral church of the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Paris. The cathedral, dedicated to the Virgin Mary (\"Our Lady\"), is considered one of the finest examples of French Gothic architecture.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Notre-Dame_de_Paris","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-85c37dc8abe4","w":889,"h":1200,"title":"Notre-Dame de Paris 2013-07-24.jpg","o":"gh-85c37dc8abe4.jpg","credit":{"text":"P e z i","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Notre-Dame_de_Paris_2013-07-24.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-bc8d100b9a94","w":1200,"h":894,"title":"Paris Cathédrale Notre-Dame Innen Langhaus Ost 2.jpg","o":"gh-bc8d100b9a94.jpg","credit":{"text":"Zairon","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paris_Cath%C3%A9drale_Notre-Dame_Innen_Langhaus_Ost_2.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-c54ab803e04b","w":904,"h":1200,"title":"NotreDameDeParis-1.jpg","o":"gh-c54ab